  "bodyTypst": "Let $f$ be the function satisfying $f'(x)= - 3 x f(x)$, for all real numbers $x$, with $f(1)= 4$ and $lim_(x -> oo) f(x)= 0$.\n\n(a) Evaluate $integral_(1)^(oo)- 3 x f(x) d x$. Show the work that leads to your answer.\n\n(b) Use Euler's method, starting at $x = 1$ with a step size of 0.5, to approximate $f(2)$.\n\n(c) Write an expression for $y = f(x)$ by solving the differential equation $frac(d y,d x)= - 3 x y$ with the initial condition $f(1)= 4$.",
